---
description: Where route UI, shared components, and lib logic live
globs: app/**/*.{ts,tsx},components/**/*.{ts,tsx},lib/**/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

# Colocation

- `app/`: route-owned UI for a single URL tree. Keep `page.tsx` focused on metadata, params, data loading, and composition. Put private route UI in `_components/` next to the route.
- `components/`: UI reused across routes or route groups, plus generic primitives with no route knowledge.
- `lib/`: data loading, CMS mapping, SEO helpers, and other non-UI logic.

## Placement checks

- Used only under one route segment? Keep it under that segment in `app/`.
- Imported from multiple routes? Move it to `components/`.
- No JSX and not route-specific presentation? Keep it in `lib/`.

## Imports

- Route files import local UI with `./_components/...`.
- Shared UI uses `@/components/...`.
- Do not import from `@/app/...` inside `components/`.
